(Bug #31 controls. These pass before and after the fix and are what pin
 the defect to pointer-backed types: a number and a boolean flag with no
 default are correct holding zero, and an explicit text default was never
 affected. Keeping them stops a future change "fixing" the wrong thing.)
a flag called retries is "-r" or "--retries", it is a number.
a flag called verbose is "-v" or "--verbose", it is a boolean.
a flag called label is "-l" or "--label", it is a text with default "xyz".
Parse flags.
Print "number:{retries}".
Print "boolean:{verbose}".
Print "text-with-default:{label}".
